    <briefdescription>
<para>K-interpolated YoY optionlet volatility. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The stripper provides curves in the T direction along each K. We don&apos;t know whether this is interpolating or fitting in the T direction. Our K direction interpolations are not model fitting.</para><para>An alternative design would be a FittedYoYOptionletVolatilitySurface taking a model, e.g. <ref refid="class_quant_lib_1_1_s_a_b_r" kindref="compound">SABR</ref> in the interest rate world. This could use the same stripping in the T direction along each K.</para><para><xrefsect id="bug_1_bug000002"><xreftitle>Bug</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>Tests currently fail. </para></xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>    </detaileddescription>
